{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1580451065,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1NTc5MzUzODg=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4110","origin":"github"},"title":"Needlessly required clone target specification?","message":"```\n% datalad clone -d analysis code\ninstall(error): ../code (dataset) [clone target path '/tmp/modules/code' not in specified target dataset '\u003cDataset path=/tmp/modules/analysis\u003e']\n```\n\nwhere both `analysis` and `code` are datasets in CWD. Works fine with an explicit target.\n\n```\n% datalad clone -d analysis code analysis/code\ninstall(ok): code (dataset)                                                                  \nadd(ok): code (file)\nadd(ok): .gitmodules (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\n```\n\nI think, without a given target, the default relpath target should be treated as relative to the target dataset (if any), and not relative to CWD.","files":null}]}